(Price is above SMA200)\n    *   RSI14: 68.78 (Approaching overbought territory, but still strong momentum)\n    *   Returns: 1m (+12.49%), 3m (+26.65%) - Strong upward trend.\n    *   P/E: Trailing 39.70, Forward 34.04 (Premium valuation, but consistent with high-growth tech).\n    *   ROE: 141.5% (Excellent profitability).\n    *   Profit Margin: 27.2% (Strong).\n    *   Revenue Growth: 16.6% (Solid).\n    *   Debt/Equity: 79.55 (Manageable).\n    *   Headlines:\n        *   Positive: Apple up 20% in 2026, looking to buy AI chip startups, India manufacturing expansion, Big Tech gains.\n        *   Neutral/Mixed: Tech stocks fall late afternoon (short-term noise), PayPal takeover (irrelevant to AAPL directly), Alibaba/Qwen AI (China market context).\n\n    *   *Bull Case:* Strong momentum (3m return +26.65%), high ROE, expansion into AI chips, and manufacturing expansion in India. The stock is trading above both major SMAs.\n    *   *Bear Case:* RSI is high (68.78), suggesting a potential pullback or consolidation soon. Forward P/E of 34 is relatively high.\n    *   *Decision:* The 6-12 month horizon favors the growth narrative (AI chips, manufacturing expansion, strong revenue growth). While the RSI is high, the trend is clearly bullish.\n\n    *   Signal: BUY\n    *   Confidence: 0.85 (High confidence due to strong fundamentals and growth narrative, slightly tempered by high RSI).\n    *   Reasoning: AAPL shows strong bullish momentum with a 26.65% 3-month return and significant growth in AI chip investments and manufacturing expansion. Despite a high RSI, the robust ROE of 141.5% and solid revenue growth support a long-term bullish outlook.\n\n    *   JSON format? Yes.\n    *   Only JSON? Yes.\n    *   One action? Yes.\n    *   Reasoning 2-4 sentences? Yes.", "finish_reason": "stop"}',91017,NULL,'2026-07-15T20:18:33+00:00');
