ove to see if the support at SMA200 holds before adding more capital, or \"BUY\" if we believe the oversold signal is the primary driver.\n    *   Actually, the prompt asks for ONE action. Since I already hold the position and the price is down significantly but showing oversold signals, \"HOLD\" is the most prudent action to wait for a trend reversal or stabilization at the SMA200. However, the prompt says \"BUY - open a position (only if you do not already hold one)\". I *do* already hold one. So the choice is between HOLD and SELL.\n    *   Is there a reason to SELL? The fundamentals (ROE 51.3%, Revenue Growth 22.2%) are very strong. The price drop seems driven by sentiment/macro (AI CapEx concerns) rather than a fundamental collapse of the company.\n    *   Decision: HOLD. The stock is oversold (RSI 29.19) and approaching long-term support (SMA200), suggesting the recent sell-off may be reaching a bottom.\n\n    *   Signal: HOLD\n    *   Confidence: 0.85\n    *   Reasoning: The stock is currently in oversold territory (RSI 29.19) and approaching significant long-term support at the SMA200 ($732.39). While recent headlines regarding AI CapEx and Baird''s downgrade have caused a sharp pullback, the strong ROE (51.3%) and revenue growth suggest underlying business strength.", "finish_reason": "stop"}',233199,NULL,'2026-07-29T21:57:11+00:00');
